[["text","LESSON 07 / 31 • ORIGINAL CHECKLIST"],["heading","7. Trees and binary search trees"],["text","English: A tree is hierarchical. A BST orders smaller keys left and larger keys right (assuming"],["text","distinct keys)."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Tree එක hierarchy එකක්. BST එJක් කුඩා keys වෙම් පැත්Jත්, J9ාකු keys දකුණු",435],["sinhala","","පැත්Jත්.",43],["text","Real-world example: Sorted product IDs"],["code","      20"],["code","     /  \\"],["code","   10    30"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","TreeSet<Integer> t = new TreeSet<>();\nt.add(20); t.add(10); t.add(30);\nSystem.out.println(t.first()); // 10"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","BST search O(h); balanced O(log n), skewed O(n). TreeSet O(log n)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Binary tree vs BST?"],["text","A binary tree has at most two children; BST also imposes key ordering."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]